                                                                                                    <em><a href="https://servicehub.amadeus.com/c/portal/view-solution/1302699762/amadeus-shopping-services-response-time-ir-36246463">Amadeus Shopping Services: Response Time : IR 36246463</a></em>
                                                                                                <br/>
                                                <br/>
                                                The following update was added:<br/>
                                                <br/>On the 26th of August, multiple customers and monitoring alarms raised critical incidents for Shopping services shortly after 11:00GMT. Customers may have experienced errors or response timeouts while conducting shopping or pricing transactions via shopping services; specifically, Flex Pricer and Master Pricer through the Amadeus Digital Commerce channels.&nbsp;<br/>

<br/>Investigations revealed an issue with the related clusters, where traffic was initially lost in the data center region. Amadeus support teams initially rerouted the traffic away from the affected server and redistributed across the remaining data center regions, subsequently increasing server resources and recycling application processes to improve performance stability.&nbsp; These actions resulted in the initial recovery of the incident at 12:26 GMT. However, at 13:27 GMT, a reoccurrence was observed as the issue began to affect the remaining regions.&nbsp;<br/>

<br/>Amadeus support teams performed multiple recovery actions in attempt to make the systems stable including recycling the affected servers, scaling up PODS, re-balanced clusters, falling back any recent implementation and also deactivate Master Pricer. Amadeus support teams reactivated the Flex Pricer traffic in related regions recovering the impact on Flex Pricer. Master Pricer traffic was gradually reactivated to avoid any sudden spikes and ensure stability. After the process was completed, positive outcomes have been observed, with some customers confirming recovery. Environments will remain under heightened monitoring, at the moment this incident has been recovered at 00:37 GMT.<br/>
